Both now return inconclusive at exit 2, naming the libraries.

compute_boundary_coverage modelled two blind spots, both at the resolution
of "did this language produce ANY call edges". Python answers that hundreds
of thousands of times on any real repo, so a clean verdict stayed
confirmable however much I/O left through an uncatalogued module. This is
the residual cli.py already recorded and pinned as an xfail, filed there as
Kotlin-specific; it is not language-specific.

The permitting case is enumerated, not the blocking one: a module supports a
clean verdict when the catalog declares a primitive for it or is_stdlib_module
knows it. A denylist would fail open on the first library nobody thought of,
which is how requests slipped through. confirmed stays reachable — a repo
whose external calls all land in known modules still confirms.

Two refinements forced by measurement, not foresight. The first draft
reported 258 modules on poetry: 231 came from imports edges (an import
performs no I/O — the catalog classifies call sites), and 120 of the
remaining 171 were poetry's OWN modules (an unresolved first-party callee is
not a catalogue gap; its source was read). supply_chain.tier cannot
discriminate those — it reads 3 for every external_symbol node — so
first-party is derived from the src side of the edge set. Filtered: 51, with
requests.Session and dulwich intact and zero poetry.*.

One predicate, both callers. catalogs is REQUIRED, not defaulted: a safety
gate that silently skips itself when a caller forgets an argument fails open
in exactly the way this exists to prevent. Module extraction reuses
_module_from_symbol_path rather than adding a seventh home (WI-ribuz).

Naming the terminal-slot set _EXTERNAL_DST_KINDS made check-symbol-kind-drift
report `unresolved` as absent from the ADR-0027 registry. The linter was right
and the name was wrong: external_symbol is a registered symbol kind,
`unresolved` is the token format_legacy_dst hardcodes. Renamed and documented;
the underlying two-vocabularies-one-slot oddity is recorded, not fixed here.

DISCLOSED RESIDUAL, pinned as a test: an edge carrying the bare `external`
placeholder names no module to adjudicate and is NOT counted. So a repo
reaching its I/O only through untyped receivers still confirms today. That
population is the receiver-typing gap (INV-linub L3).

NOT MEASURED: any non-Python language; the false-downgrade direction beyond
the fixtures and these two repos.

